-- title:
--   Node annuli and crossing data over a supersingular place
-- statement:
--   **Setting.** Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$, and write $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A`. Inside the Laurent series over $\kappa$ let `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` be the $\kappa$-subfield generated by `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`; `W` is a finite set of places of this field over $\kappa$ whose members are exactly the elements of `ssPlaces q M' κ` (hypothesis `hW`), that is, the places $w$ that are rational (the structure map from $\kappa$ to the residue field of $w$ is onto), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M'`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at `jGeomGen κ M'` $=$ `jqModC κ` lies in `ssJSet q κ`; and $s$ is a chosen element of `W`. Further, `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H=$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; the hypothesis `hle` states that the base change `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` of the full level-$M'$ modular function field is contained in it, and `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` denotes that inclusion. Finally, `R₀` is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with residue field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ through the constants, together with the place map and divisor-degree clauses of that structure), and `hR₀` says that it is coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in the Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its `R₀`-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. An element $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ is fixed.
--
--   **Data.** A field `FSS` over $\kappa$ containing a transcendental element (hypothesis `h0`); a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with residue field `FSS` (a valuation subring `R.integers`, a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, with the scaling clause); a finite set $N$ of places of `FSS` over $\kappa$ with $|N|=q+1$ (`hcard`); and, indexed by the places $Q$ of `FSS` over $\kappa$, subrings `Sx Q` of `fieldBar q M'`, ring maps `φx Q : Polynomial ↥A →+* ↥(Sx Q)`, characters `χ₀x Q : ↥(Sx Q) →+* κ`, and sets `Dx Q` of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   Throughout, say that a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ *lies over $s$* if for every $f\in$ `R₀.integers` which has nonnegative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$ has nonnegative order, and whose `R₀`-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals the value at $s$ of that `R₀`-residue, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ minus $a$ lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **Hypotheses on $R$ and the smooth-point data.** `h1` ($R$ lies over $s$): for $f\in$ `R₀.integers` regular wherever $j$ is and with `R₀`-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ lies in `R.integers` and its $R$-residue is the image in `FSS` of the value at $s$ of that residue. `h2`: `R.integers` is stable under all level automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. `hpkg` (smooth-point packages): for every place $Q\notin N$ the quadruple $(S_Q,\varphi_Q,\chi_{0,Q},D_Q)=$ (`Sx Q`, `φx Q`, `χ₀x Q`, `Dx Q`) satisfies the fourteen clauses that constitute an étale chart with its residue disc, namely: the constants from $A$ lie in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ is the constant $a$ and $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$; $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(X))=0$; for each $c\in A$ with zero residue there is exactly one $A$-section $\chi:S_Q\to A$ of $\varphi_Q$ on constants with residue $\chi_{0,Q}$ and $\chi(\varphi_Q(X))=c$; every element of $S_Q$ lies in `R.integers`, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and reduces there to the image of $\chi_{0,Q}$ of the element; the order at $Q$ of the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q(X)$ is $1$; $D_Q$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ at which all of $S_Q$ is defined with values in $A$, and for which $A$-valuation of the value at $P$ is $<1$ precisely for the elements killed by $\chi_{0,Q}$; each section $\chi$ as above is the evaluation at a unique $P\in D_Q$; for $P\in D_Q$ the valuation subring of $P$ is the set of quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in S_Q$, $h(P)\neq0$; any nonzero element of the field with all orders $0$ on $D_Q$ becomes, after multiplication by a nonzero constant, a unit of $S_Q$; and every element of `R.integers` lying in all the valuation subrings of $D_Q$ belongs to $S_Q$. `hdisj`: for $Q,Q'\notin N$, a place lying in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$ forces $Q=Q'$. `hcusp`: for $Q\notin N$ every $P\in D_Q$ has nonnegative order at the image of $j$. `heqv`: for $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` ($\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$) which preserves `R.integers`, the induced residue automorphism `R.resAut τ hτ` preserves $N$ (membership is equivalent), and for $Q\notin N$ one has `smulDisc τ (Dx Q) = Dx (R.resAut τ hτ • Q)`, where `smulDisc τ D` $=\{P\mid \tau^{-1}\cdot P\in D\}$. `hUniq`: for $Q\notin N$, any quadruple $(S,\varphi,\chi_0,D)$ satisfying the same fourteen clauses has $D=D_Q$, $S=S_Q$ and $\chi_0=\chi_{0,Q}$ on $S$.
--
--   **The node hypothesis `hC2a`.** It asserts the existence of a finite set $N'$ of $q+1$ places of `FSS` over $\kappa$ together with: for each place $x$ a field `FIx x` over $\kappa$, a regular prolongation `Rx x` of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with residue field `FIx x` and a place `bx x` of `FIx x` over $\kappa$ (the second branch at a node); an index type $\Lambda$, subrings `C' l` of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ contained in $A$, each a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with elements `ϖ' l` and a base index $l_0$; commutative domains `Wc l` that are adically complete discrete valuation rings, elements `πW l`, exponents `E l` and $E_0$; sets `S nd` of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, subrings `𝒩 nd` and local noetherian subrings `𝒩₀ nd l`, and elements `cx nd`, `cy nd`, `cu nd` of `fieldBar q M'`; subject to the following clauses. Global clauses: an element of `C' l` has zero residue in $\kappa$ exactly when it is divisible by `ϖ' l`; `C' l₀ ≤ C' l` for all $l$; `ϖ' l₀` is nonzero; every element of $A$ is algebraic over `C' l₀`; each `πW l` is irreducible and $1\le$ `E l`; every element of the inertia subgroup `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` with trivial tame character `A.tameCharacter π τ = 1` fixes `ϖ' l₀`; and `(ϖ' l₀)^E₀` equals a unit of $A$ times $\pi^{w}$ for some $w\ge 1$. Clauses for each $nd\in N'$: `bx nd`, $nd$ and all places of `S nd` are rational; `𝒩 nd` consists of the elements lying in `(Rx nd).integers`, in `R.integers` and in all valuation subrings of `S nd`, and such elements take values in $A$ at the places of `S nd`; the crossing relation `cx nd * cy nd = (ϖ' l₀)^E₀ * cu nd`; the $(Rx\,nd)$-residue of `cx nd` is $0$ while the order at $nd$ of its $R$-residue is $1$, and symmetrically the $R$-residue of `cy nd` is $0$ while the order at `bx nd` of its $(Rx\,nd)$-residue is $1$; for $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup with trivial tame character, the semilinear automorphism [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')) τ`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) preserves `S nd` and fixes `cx nd` and `cy nd`; every element of the field is a quotient of elements of some `𝒩₀ nd l`, and becomes, after multiplication by a nonzero element of `𝒩₀ nd l₀`, a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-linear combination of elements of `𝒩₀ nd l₀`; and, for every $l$: `𝒩₀ nd l₀ ≤ 𝒩₀ nd l ≤ 𝒩 nd`; `S nd` is exactly the set of places at which all of `𝒩₀ nd l` is defined and all non-units of `𝒩₀ nd l` take values in the maximal ideal of $A$; `C' l` maps into `𝒩₀ nd l`; every element of `𝒩₀ nd l` differs from the image of some element of `C' l` by a non-unit; $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-families that are `C' l`-linearly independent admit no nontrivial relation with coefficients in `𝒩₀ nd l`; there is a subring `Bx` of the field inside `𝒩₀ nd l`, containing `cx nd`, `cy nd`, `cu nd`, such that `𝒩₀ nd l` is obtained from `Bx` by inverting those of its elements that are units of `𝒩₀ nd l`, and `Bx` is generated by the image of `C' l` together with a finite set; `cx nd`, `cy nd` lie in `𝒩₀ nd l` and `cu nd` is a unit there; and there are a ring map $\sigma$ from `Wc l` to the adic completion of `𝒩₀ nd l` at its maximal ideal and a ring isomorphism $\iota$ of that completion with `UVCrossingModel (Wc l) (πW l ^ E l)` $=$ `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) (Wc l)` modulo $(X_0X_1-$ `πW l ^ E l`$)$, such that $\sigma($`πW l`$)$ is the image of `ϖ' l`, $\iota\circ\sigma$ is `const`, the images of `C' l` lie in the image of $\sigma$, and orders are read off on the two branches: an element of `𝒩₀ nd l` whose $(Rx\,nd)$-residue is nonzero of order $n$ at `bx nd` has $\iota$-image congruent to a unit times `V (πW l ^ E l) ^ n` modulo the ideal spanned by `const (πW l ^ E l) (πW l)` and `U (πW l ^ E l)`, and symmetrically with $R$, $nd$, `U`$^n$ and the ideal spanned by `const` and `V`. Remaining clauses of `hC2a`: the sets `S nd` ($nd\in N'$) are pairwise disjoint; every $P\in$ `S nd` lies over $s$; for each $\zeta'\in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ there is a self-map $\tau_N$ of the places of `FSS` carrying $N'$ into itself, transporting the sets `S nd` along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` and matching `(Rx nd).integers` with `(Rx (τN nd)).integers` under comap along that automorphism; for $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms preserving `R.integers`, `R.resAut τ hτ` preserves $N'$ and `smulDisc τ (S nd) = S (R.resAut τ hτ • nd)`; the image of `R₀.integers` lies in `(Rx nd).integers`; for each $nd\in N'$ there is a ring map $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` to `FIx nd` compatible with the two residue maps and such that membership in the valuation subring of $s$ corresponds to membership in that of `bx nd`; a Hasse datum for the invariant `jqNModC ℚ̄ q` (the series $j$ in $q^{q}$): it lies in `fieldBar q M'`, there is $a_0\in A$ with `jqNModC ℚ̄ q` $-a_0$ in `R.integers` of $R$-residue $0$ and with $(\mathrm{res}\,a_0)^q$ equal to the value at $s$ of `jGeomGen κ M'`, and a scalar $c'$ with $c'\cdot($`jqNModC ℚ̄ q`$-a_0)$ in `R.integers` of nonzero residue such that for each $nd\in N'$ the difference lies in `(Rx nd).integers` with nonzero residue and the order at $nd$ of the $R$-residue of the scaled difference is the negative of the order at `bx nd` of the $(Rx\,nd)$-residue of the difference; two separation clauses, namely that for $x\in N'$ and $y\notin N'$ there is $g\in$ `R.integers` $\cap$ `𝒩₀ x l₀` which is a non-unit there, has nonzero $R$-residue of order $0$ at $y$, and is defined at every rational place where $j$ is regular, and that for distinct $x,x'\in N'$ there is $g$ equal to `cx x` times a unit in `𝒩₀ x l₀` and a unit in `𝒩₀ x' l₀`; and a dichotomy: every rational place lying over $s$ either belongs to some `S nd` with $nd\in N'$ or belongs to a set $D$ for which `R.IsResidueDisc Q D z` holds for some $Q\notin N'$ and some $z$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a family `An` assigning to each place of `FSS` over $\kappa$ an `Annulus A (fieldBar q M')` — a set `dom` of places, a parameter `param` and a modulus in the maximal ideal of $A$, subject to the axioms of that structure: the places of `dom` are rational, `param` is defined there with value a nonzero element of the maximal ideal dividing the modulus, each admissible value of `param` is attained at exactly one place of `dom`, the order of `param` minus its value is $1$, and the unit principle for functions without zeros on `dom` — such that the following hold.
--
--   1.
--
--   For every $x\in N$: (a) `(An x).param` lies in `R.integers`, the order at $x$ of its $R$-residue is $1$, and for every $f\in$ `R.integers` with nonzero $R$-residue and with order $0$ at all $P\in$ `(An x).dom`, the product of the value of $f$ at $P$ with the value of `(An x).param` at $P$ raised to the power $-x.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in $A$ and is a unit there, for every $P\in$ `(An x).dom`; (b) `(An x).modulus` is nonzero in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; (c) for every $Q\notin N$, no $P\in$ `(An x).dom` lies in `Dx Q`; (d) every $P\in$ `(An x).dom` lies over $s$.
--
--   2.
--
--   For $x,x'\in N$, a place lying in both `(An x).dom` and `(An x').dom` forces $x=x'$.
--
--   3.
--
--   For $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` ($\zeta\in$ `Idx q`, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$) which preserves `R.integers`, and for $x\in N$: `smulDisc τ (An x).dom = (An (R.resAut τ hτ • x)).dom`.
--
--   4.
--
--   Every rational place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that lies over $s$ either lies in `Dx Q` for some $Q\notin N$ or lies in `(An x).dom` for some $x\in N$.
--
--   5.
--
--   For distinct $x,x'\in N$ there is $g\in$ `R.integers` with nonzero $R$-residue, with nonzero order of that residue at $x$, with order $0$ at every $P\in$ `(An x).dom`, and such that at every $P\in$ `(An x').dom` the element $g$ is defined and its value is a unit of $A$.
--
--   6.
--
--   A node package over $N$: there exist data `FIx`, `Rx`, `bx`, $\Lambda$, `C'` with `ϖ'` and $l_0$, `Wc` with `πW`, `E`, $E_0$, and `S`, `𝒩`, `𝒩₀`, `cx`, `cy`, `cu` of exactly the same shape as in `hC2a`, satisfying the same global clauses (residue criterion for `ϖ' l`, monotonicity of the `C' l`, `ϖ' l₀` nonzero, algebraicity of $A$ over `C' l₀`, irreducibility of `πW l` and $1\le$ `E l`, inertia invariance of `ϖ' l₀`, and `(ϖ' l₀)^E₀` $=$ unit times $\pi^w$ with $w\ge1$), the same clauses for every $nd\in N$ (rationality, the description of `𝒩 nd` and integrality of values on `S nd`, the crossing relation between `cx`, `cy`, `cu`, the four branch-order clauses, inertia invariance of `S nd`, `cx nd`, `cy nd`, the two generation clauses, and, for each $l$, the whole per-level block: inclusions, the valuative description of `S nd`, the constants from `C' l`, the residue-field clause, linear independence, the finitely generated subring `Bx` with its localisation, membership and unit statements for `cx`, `cy`, `cu`, and the pair $(\sigma,\iota)$ identifying the adic completion of `𝒩₀ nd l` with `UVCrossingModel (Wc l) (πW l ^ E l)` together with the two order-detection clauses in `U` and `V`), the Hasse datum for `jqNModC ℚ̄ q` with $a_0$, $c'$ and the order relation at every $nd\in N$, the pairwise disjointness of the sets `S nd`, the statement that every $P\in$ `S nd` lies over $s$, the level-automorphism permutation clause with its map $\tau_N$ on $N$, the `R.resAut` clause with `smulDisc τ (S nd) = S (R.resAut τ hτ • nd)`, the inclusion of the image of `R₀.integers` in `(Rx nd).integers`, and the existence for each $nd\in N$ of the comparison map $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` to `FIx nd` compatible with residues and matching the valuation subring of $s$ with that of `bx nd`; and, in addition, the identification `S nd = (An nd).dom` for every $nd\in N$. The two separation clauses and the dichotomy of `hC2a` are not among the conjuncts of this existential statement; they are reflected in conjuncts 4 and 5 above.
--
--   This is the node half of the construction of the semistable model of the full-level curve $X_H(q^2M')$, with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$, above a supersingular point $s$ of $X_0(M')$ in characteristic $q$: the $q+1$ branches meeting at the supersingular nodes are packaged as annuli whose domains are the node domains $S$, disjoint from the smooth residue discs, permuted by the level automorphisms, and carrying cross units and the Hasse datum on the invariant $j(\mathsf q^{\,q})$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_nodePresentations_crossUnits_igusaOverS_inertia_nodeCharts_hasseJ`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_nodePresentations_crossUnits_igusaOverS_inertia_nodeCharts_hasseJ).
